================================================================================
  TETONIC SOFTWARE LICENSE AGREEMENT
================================================================================

Tetonic Labs LLC offers this software under a community and commercial model
modeled on modern developer platforms (such as the Docker subscription model):
free for individuals, educational use, open source, and small businesses, with
a paid commercial subscription required for larger organizations.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SUMMARY OF PERMITTED USE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

| User / Organization Type | Terms |
|---|---|
| **Personal Use** | **100% Free** for personal projects and hobbies. |
| **Education & Non-Profit Academic** | **100% Free** for students, faculty, and academic research. |
| **Open Source Contributors** | **100% Free** for non-commercial open source development. |
| **Small Businesses & Startups** | **100% Free** for internal and commercial production use if your organization has: <br> (1) 10 or fewer software developers; AND <br> (2) Less than $2,000,000 USD in annual revenue / ARR. |
| **Evaluation Period** | **Free 30-Day Trial** for any organization of any size to test, evaluate, and benchmark internally. |
| **Large Organizations & Enterprises** | **Paid Commercial Subscription Required** for organizations with more than 10 developers OR $2,000,000+ USD in annual revenue/ARR after the 30-day evaluation period. |
| **Cloud / Managed Service Providers** | **Restricted**: You may not offer the software as a commercial hosted service or cloud API to third parties without an agreement. |

Commercial Licensing and Inquiries:
    Contact: enterprise@tetonic.ai

================================================================================
  LICENSE TERMS AND CONDITIONS
================================================================================

1. DEFINITIONS

   (a) "Licensor" means Tetonic Labs LLC.

   (b) "Licensed Work" means the Tetonic software platform, the Lokai coding
       assistant, the Mantle fleet orchestrator, and all source code, documentation,
       APIs, and binaries provided in this repository.

   (c) "Entity" means the individual or legal entity using the Licensed Work,
       together with all Affiliates under common control as a consolidated whole.
       "Affiliate" means any entity that directly or indirectly controls, is
       controlled by, or is under common control with the user (where "control"
       means 50% or more ownership or voting power).

   (d) "Developer" means any employee, contractor, or consultant who writes,
       edits, reviews, tests, or maintains software, code, prompts, or technical
       infrastructure on behalf of the Entity.

   (e) "Annual Revenue" means the total consolidated annual revenue, gross
       receipts, or Annual Recurring Revenue (ARR) of the Entity and all Affiliates
       in its most recent fiscal year.

   (f) "Small Business" means an Entity that simultaneously satisfies both:
       (1) It engages ten (10) or fewer total Developers across the entire
           organization; AND
       (2) Its Annual Revenue is less than two million U.S. dollars ($2,000,000 USD).

   (g) "Commercial Subscription" means a valid, active commercial enterprise
       subscription agreement executed between the Entity and Tetonic Labs LLC.


2. GRANT OF LICENSE FOR PERMITTED FREE USES

   Subject to the terms of this Agreement, Licensor grants you a non-exclusive,
   worldwide, royalty-free license to copy, modify, distribute, display, and use
   the Licensed Work for the following Permitted Free Uses:

   (a) Personal Use: Use by an individual for personal, non-commercial purposes,
       hobbies, and side projects.

   (b) Educational Use: Use by students, teachers, and faculty at accredited,
       non-profit academic institutions for educational instruction and non-commercial
       academic research.

   (c) Non-Commercial Open Source: Use for developing and maintaining non-commercial,
       public open-source software projects.

   (d) Small Business Use: Internal development, testing, and commercial production
       use by a Small Business (10 or fewer developers and under $2M ARR).

   (e) Evaluation Use: Internal testing and evaluation of the Licensed Work by an
       Entity of any size for a temporary period not to exceed thirty (30) days,
       for the sole purpose of evaluating whether to purchase a Commercial
       Subscription.


3. COMMERCIAL SUBSCRIPTION REQUIRED FOR ENTERPRISE USE

   Any use of the Licensed Work by an Entity that is not a Small Business (i.e.,
   any organization that employs or contracts more than ten (10) Developers OR
   has Annual Revenue of two million U.S. dollars ($2,000,000 USD) or more)
   requires a paid Commercial Subscription from Tetonic Labs LLC following the
   expiration of the 30-day Evaluation period.

   Thresholds apply to the Entity as a whole, including all Affiliates. Organizations
   may not segment internal departments, divisions, or subsidiaries to claim Small
   Business status.


4. RESTRICTIONS

   Except as expressly authorized under a Commercial Subscription, you shall not:

   (a) Commercial Hosting: Provide the Licensed Work, or any substantially similar
       service derived from it, as a hosted service, managed service, cloud platform,
       software-as-a-service (SaaS), or commercial web API to third parties.

   (b) Notice Removal: Remove, alter, or obscure any copyright, trademark, patent,
       or attribution notices contained in the Licensed Work.

   (c) Model Training: Use the Licensed Work, its prompts, system instructions,
       or outputs to train, fine-tune, or distill competing commercial artificial
       intelligence foundation models or coding assistants without an explicit
       agreement.


5. FOUR-YEAR OPEN SOURCE CONVERSION

   Licensor commits to the long-term open-source availability of the software.
   Four (4) years after the initial public release date of each specific version
   of the Licensed Work, that version automatically converts to and is licensed
   under the terms of the Apache License, Version 2.0.


6. TERM, TERMINATION, AND CURE PERIOD

   (a) This Agreement remains in effect until terminated.

   (b) If an Entity uses the Licensed Work outside the scope of the Permitted Free
       Uses without an active Commercial Subscription, Licensor may notify the
       Entity in writing. The Entity shall have thirty (30) days from receipt of
       such notice to cure the non-compliance by purchasing a Commercial Subscription
       or ceasing use.

   (c) If the non-compliance is not cured within the 30-day cure period, all rights
       under this Agreement terminate automatically, and the Entity must cease all
       use of the Licensed Work.


7. INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY

   All title, ownership rights, and intellectual property rights in and to the
